// Reactivity S4b — the owner tree composes with `computed`. A computed creates a child effect during
// its body, so it OWNS that child; when the computed recomputes it disposes the prior child first. An
// outer effect reads the computed (forcing it), and changing the computed's dependency `src` reruns the
// outer effect, which re-reads and recomputes the computed — tearing down the old child effect and
// making a new one. A change to `dep` then reruns the single live child, not one per stale recompute.
//
//   first flush : outer reads c → c computes, creates child#1 → "owned dep=0"
//   src.set(1)  : outer reruns → c recomputes → dispose child#1, create child#2 → "owned dep=0"
//   dep.set(3)  : only child#2 is live → "owned dep=3" ONCE
// expect: stdout "owned dep=0"
// expect: stdout "owned dep=0"
// expect: stdout "owned dep=3"
// expect: stdout "done"
// expect: exit 0
use std.reactive.{signal, computed, effect}
src = signal(0)
dep = signal(0)
c = computed(fn() {
    effect(fn() {
        echo "owned dep=${dep.get()}"
    })
    src.get()
})
effect(fn() {
    c.get()
})
src.set(1)
dep.set(3)
echo "done"
